<title>RUSSIA: Russia's Avtobank gets $50 mln foreign credit.</title>
<headline>Russia's Avtobank gets $50 mln foreign credit.</headline>
<dateline>MOSCOW 1997-06-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>One of Russia's biggest banks, Avtobank, signed a $50 million syndicated credit agreement with a group of foreign banks led by CitiBank, an Avtobank official said on Friday.</p>
<p>Spokesman Alexander Tkachyov told Reuters the credit was granted at LIBOR plus four percent.</p>
<p>He said Avtobank would get the first $25 million tranche by June 23 and would get the rest by July 5.</p>
<p>--Alexei Pankratov, Moscow Newsroom, +7095 941 8520</p>
</text>
